# The Frog King's theme, from AXI. Plays when Maisie walks into his arena.
#
# D minor against the overworld's C major, and it MARCHES where that one skips.
# The difference is the point: a boss you can hear coming should not sound like
# the walk that got you there. Long held notes with a dotted lift into each
# bar, a bass hammering root and fifth, and a kick on all four beats.
#
# Eight bars, same shape as the overworld theme, so the crossfade between them
# lands on a phrase rather than across one.
#
# D minor, 96 BPM, 8 bars, 4/4. 16bit: this is the era AXI ships.

@track boss-king-axi
  name   THE FROG KING (AXI)
  bpm    96
  beats  16
  era    16bit
  tags   axi game boss original

# The fanfare. It climbs for four bars, turns at the top and comes back down,
# which is a frog getting bigger and then sitting on you.
@voice lead inst=lead-echo mix=0.20
  d5  .   .   .   d5  .   f5  .   a5  .   .   .   a5  .   .   .
  a5  .   g#5 .   a5  .   .   .   f5  .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  a#4 .   .   .   a#4 .   d5  .   f5  .   .   .   f5  .   .   .
  e5  .   .   .   e5  .   .   .   c#5 .   .   .   a4  .   .   .
  d5  .   .   .   f5  .   .   .   a5  .   .   .   d6  .   .   .
  c6  .   a#5 .   a5  .   .   .   g5  .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  f5  .   .   .   f5  .   g5  .   a5  .   .   .   a#5 .   .   .
  a5  .   .   .   e5  .   .   .   c#5 .   .   .   d5  .   .   .

# Held, not arpeggiated. The overworld's chord moves on every sixteenth and
# that is what makes it bright; this one sits still and lets the bass do the
# work, which is what makes it heavy.
@voice pad inst=arp mix=0.045
  dm  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  dm  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  bb  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  a   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  dm  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  gm  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  bb  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  a   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .

# Root and fifth, on the beat, over and over. No octave jumps and no walking:
# the overworld bass is a bounce and this one is a footfall.
@voice bass inst=tri mix=0.21
  d2  .   d2  .   a2  .   a2  .   d2  .   d2  .   a2  .   a2  .
  d2  .   d2  .   a2  .   a2  .   d2  .   d2  .   a2  .   d3  .
  a#1 .   a#1 .   f2  .   f2  .   a#1 .   a#1 .   f2  .   f2  .
  a1  .   a1  .   e2  .   e2  .   a1  .   a1  .   e2  .   a2  .
  d2  .   d2  .   a2  .   a2  .   d2  .   d2  .   a2  .   a2  .
  g1  .   g1  .   d2  .   d2  .   g1  .   g1  .   d2  .   d2  .
  a#1 .   a#1 .   f2  .   f2  .   a#1 .   a#1 .   f2  .   f2  .
  a1  .   a1  .   e2  .   e2  .   a1  .   a1  .   e2  .   e2  .

# Four on the floor, and a roll into the turn at the end of bars four and eight.
@voice drums inst=kit mix=0.125
  k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .   k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .
  k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .   k   .   .   .   s   .   k   .
  k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .   k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .
  k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .   k   .   .   .   x   x   t   x
  k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .   k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .
  k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .   k   .   .   .   s   .   k   .
  k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .   k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .
  k   .   .   .   s   .   .   .   x   x   x   x   t   t   t   x
